## 6. Layout & Breakpoints

### Breakpoints (CSS variables in `base.css`)

| Token | Value | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| `--breakpoint-sm` | `768px` | `min-width` tablet up |
| `--breakpoint-md` | `1024px` | tablet max / desktop split |

- Mobile: `max-width: calc(var(--breakpoint-sm) - 1px)` (i.e. &lt; 768px).
- Tablet range: `min-width: var(--breakpoint-sm)` and `max-width: var(--breakpoint-md)`.
- Desktop: `min-width: calc(var(--breakpoint-md) + 1px)` (i.e. &gt; 1024px).

### Layout

| Token | Value | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `--layout-container` | `1440px` | Full-page max |
| `--layout-content` | `1280px` | Standard content (e.g. `.l-container`) |
| `--layout-prose` | `1120px` | Text-heavy columns |
| `--layout-mobile` | `375px` | SP baseline |
| `--layout-mobile-content` | `335px` | SP content |
| `--layout-mobile-narrow` | `280px` | SP narrow readable |
| `--layout-padding-inline` | `80px` | Horizontal page padding (desktop) |
| `--layout-padding-inline-mobile` | `20px` | Horizontal page padding (mobile) |

