## 7. Component Naming Convention

BEM-like pattern — mandatory:

```
.c-[component]
.c-[component]__element
.c-[component]--modifier
```

---

## 8. Component Quick Rules

- **Button**: Primary / Accent / Outline / Pill. Main nav CTA uses Pill.
- **Header/Footer CTA**: Pill style, brand-consistent.
- **Breadcrumb**: `14px`, `line-height: 20px`, `--color-text-secondary`.
- **Label/Tag**: Helvetica, `16px`, Bold, `line-height: 32px`.
- **Pagination**: number / prev / next distinction; active uses `--color-primary`.
- **Floating CTA**: Pill + subtle shadow for visibility.
- **Card structure**: thumbnail, category, title, description, link.
- CTA ring/border effect via `box-shadow` or pseudo-element, NOT thick border hacks.
- Do not overuse gradients on small components.

---

## 9. Implementation Notes

- `box-shadow` or pseudo-element for CTA outer ring — no border hacks.
- Avoid gradient backgrounds on small components.
- Prioritize spacing that prevents layout breakage as content grows.
- Header/Footer main nav buttons: **pill style** on both PC and SP.
- `rgba(...)` inside SVG `data:` URIs cannot use CSS variables — keep hex there,
  but ensure the hex matches a token color.

---

## Validation Checklist

Before completing any component:

- [ ] All colors reference `var(--color-*)` tokens (no hex in property values).
- [ ] Border-radius uses only `--radius-sm/md/lg/pill`.
- [ ] Spacing uses only approved scale values.
- [ ] Typography follows font-family, size, weight, line-height rules.
- [ ] Heading sizes follow PC/SP responsive mapping.
- [ ] Container/content width matches page context.
- [ ] SP layout uses approved mobile widths.
- [ ] Responsive behavior preserves readability (no aggressive font shrinking).
- [ ] BEM naming convention followed: `.c-[name]__element--modifier`.
- [ ] CSS mirrored: `assets/css/` -> `development-dev/assets/css/`.
